<!--
  The themed-icon layer: a true single-colour silhouette.

  This exists because the monochrome slot used to point at the full-colour
  foreground. Android tints whatever it finds there with one colour, so a
  multi-colour drawable does not become a nice monochrome version of itself —
  gradients and alpha flatten into a smear. A themed icon needs a mask that was
  drawn as a mask.

  The flame is outlined rather than solid so it stays recognisable when the
  system floods it with a single tone. The spread beneath it cannot use the
  foreground's alpha trick for the same reason — one tone means the two leaves
  would fuse into a slab — so the valley between them is widened from 2 units to
  3 and each leaf is inset, which keeps the spine readable as a shape rather
  than as a difference in lightness.
-->
